<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mikulov</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nikolsburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mikulov, German Nikolsburg, is a town in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a> near the Austrian border, known for its castle, its vineyards and its historic Jewish community, long the seat of the chief rabbi of Moravia. The castle was held by the Dietrichstein family from 1575. In July 1866 the preliminary peace ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-prussian-war">Austro-Prussian War</a> was signed there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mikulov.jpg" alt="Mikulov" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Juhele_CZ · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2019-11-06_13-04-11_Pentax_JH.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
